> - Per k-stratum medians: k=2: 4.26x (sig_loss 8.6%); k=3: 3.64x (12.9%); k=4-5: 3.10x (13.1%); k=6-9: 3.18x (17.3%); k>=10: 3.80x (25.1%). sig_loss increases with k because higher-k pooled effects sit closer to null, so floor widening crosses zero more often.
